2026-09-01T12:28Z claude note DESIGN CHOICES worth the author's eye. (1) Two SPEC traps are now unrepresentable rather than documented: `libraries` CHECKs that a `fulltext_watermark` is NULL unless the scope is cloud (§5.2.4(2)'s mixed local sequence), and `cursors` CHECKs that no row is named `fulltext` so the generic table cannot serve as the back door. (2) Priority is one indexed ORDER BY over a STORED generated `class_rank` column — no scheduler object, per Action 1; `nextWorkOrder` takes a lane filter rather than arbitrating, because the r = 3 interleave is the conductor choosing which lane to ask. (3) The tick's item read is `?since=` on `/items`, NOT on `?format=versions`, and the redundancy with the deletion census is deliberate: only the data read carries `dateAdded` and `itemType`, which are the newest-first sort key and the discovery class. Collapsing the two reads saves one request and costs the ordering. (4) Back-off doubles from 60 s and caps at FIVE minutes, not the usual fifteen, because the ceiling is what bounds how long after Zotero returns the tick notices — i.e. the ceiling is R35's recovery time. Closing that properly wants a cheap liveness probe on its own cadence, which belongs to the tranche that wires the conductor loop; disclosed, not solved

2026-09-01T12:28Z claude note ACTION 3(a) DEVIATION, flagged rather than glossed: the canned responses are NOT captured from the author's profile — no local Zotero was reachable from this session. They are synthesized to the wire shape verified by reading `src/api/local-client.ts` (the `format=versions` object, the data-wrapped `/items` array, the `Total-Results` / `Last-Modified-Version` headers, the 404-means-no-fulltext contract, the `/file` redirect). The fake is a real record/replay pair: `recorder(realFetch)` passes calls through to a live Zotero and captures them into the same route table `put()` fills, and `cassette()` / `load()` round-trip it — so one run against the author's profile replaces the synthesized set with a real one and no test changes. Until that run happens the shapes are read off the client, not off Zotero

2026-09-01T12:28Z claude note POSITIVE CONTROLS, all executed, all red before green. Fixture (a) replay fake: re-canning the same route changes the answer (proving it serves the cassette rather than a fixed thing), and an unregistered route throws instead of answering 404 — the 404 reading is the dangerous one, since a mistyped route would surface as "this attachment has no full text", a plausible silent negative. Fixture (b) synthetic library: `assertInvariants()` was run against five deliberate corruptions — reordered dateAdded, an orphaned child note, a census naming a non-item, the version-0 residue stamped away, the monster attachment flattened — and threw on each. Fixture (c) clock: it refuses to run backwards, and the tick was run with the clock NOT advanced, where `runIfDue` returns undefined and nothing fires. Beyond the fixtures, SIX MUTANTS were run against the tick implementation and each killed exactly the test that should have caught it: deletion subtraction removed, the item-version half of the full-text signal dropped, the full-text diff always firing, the discovery class collapsed to metadata, a document fetch injected into the tick, and the back-off flattened to the cadence. The document-fetch mutant matters most — "never fetches a document" is a NEGATIVE assertion, worth nothing until something makes it fire, and it fired

2026-09-01T12:28Z claude note VERSION-0 RESIDUE, both halves implemented and both tested. Resolution (i): the census diff compares `(fulltext version, attachment item version)`, so replacing a file — which bumps the attachment item in the sequence the tick already sweeps — is caught for free; tested, the tick discovers it. Resolution (ii): a local re-extraction that re-stamps 0 with no file change is invisible, and the test asserts exactly that blindness rather than papering over it — the tick reports zero changes and enqueues nothing. What makes it a disclosure rather than a silent hole is `TickReport.versionZeroResidue`, the count of census entries stamped 0, which is the number the contract sentence "version-0 text refreshes on file change or rebuild" is measured against. Resolutions (iii) and (iv) are out of scope by the ticket's own text

